# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 OR MIT
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use jspassgen-sdk-rust in research or production write-ups, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "jspassgen-sdk-rust: a native Rust port of the jspassgen password generator core"
abstract: >-
  The Rust member of the jspassgen suite: a native port of the jspassgen
  core that generates passwords in the caller's process from the
  operating system's CSPRNG, with no network call and no telemetry. It
  currently provides the random source; the generators follow the
  jspassgen conformance kit.
authors:
  - family-names: Rousseau
    given-names: Sebastien
version: "0.0.23"
# Dual-licensed, at the user's option (LICENSE-APACHE, LICENSE-MIT). CFF
# 1.2.0 takes SPDX licence identifiers, not an SPDX expression; a list of
# several means the work is available under any of them.
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sebastienrousseau/jspassgen-sdk-rust"
url: "https://jspassgen.com"
keywords:
  - password
  - passphrase
  - CSPRNG
  - Rust
